    options: [
      { label: 'Fold QTo from CO (or call if first caller)', isCorrect: true, explanation: 'QTo from CO facing BTN open is marginal. 3-betting QTo OOP (CO is OOP vs BTN) is generally EV-. QTo is too strong to be a typical 3-bet bluff like A5s/76s (bluffs want blockers or suited draws), but too weak to be 3-bet value. Fold or call based on relative position.' },
      { label: 'Polarized 3-bet with QTo as a bluff', isCorrect: false, explanation: 'QTo is not a good 3-bet bluff candidate. The best bluffs have blockers (Ax) or realized equity potential (suited connectors). QTo has good equity but realizes it better by calling than 3-betting.' },
      { label: 'Linear 3-bet with QTo for value', isCorrect: false, explanation: 'QTo is not a value 3-bet hand from CO vs BTN. The value 3-bet range from CO starts at approximately QQ+, AK, AQ with the best suited connectors.' },
      { label: 'Always 3-bet to take initiative', isCorrect: false, explanation: 'Taking initiative systematically is not an EV+ strategy. Each 3-bet must be justified by equity, blockers, or position.' },
    ],
    lesson: '3-bet ranges are divided into value (QQ+, AKs, AQs+) and bluffs (A5s, A4s, suited connectors with blockers). QTo is in the no-man land — too strong to be a good bluff, too weak to be value from OOP. Call or fold based on situation.',
