    lesson: 'When a solver mixes a strong hand, it signals that the range advantage is not sufficient to bet 100%. On A♣J♥9♣, BB can have many strong hands (JJ, 99, AJ), reducing the 3-bettor\'s advantage. The mix balances ranges and maximizes EV in this context of uncertainty.',
